<title>USA: US Treasury 5-year notes seen yielding 6.67 pct.</title>
<headline>US Treasury 5-year notes seen yielding 6.67 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's auction of $12.5 billion in five-year notes Wednesday is expected to produce a yield near 6.67 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 1237 EST/1737 GMT, yields on the five-year notes were quoted at 6.672 percent in when-issued trade.</p>
<p>The bidding deadline for the notes is 1300 EST/1800 GMT. Results are expected around 1345 EST/1845 GMT.</p>
<p>((--John P. Hughes, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1663))</p>
</text>
